/* Internet Sharing path: skip DHCP (mDNS jams RX) and go static.
   On the sharing Mac, while this runs:
	ifconfig | grep -A5 'inet 192.168.2'
	sudo tcpdump -n -i bridge100 arp or host 192.168.2.50
   (interface may be enX ù use the USB LAN or bridge100)

   If tcpdump shows no ARP from 38:c9:86:4e:94:cb ? TX not on wire.
   If Mac replies but ZealOS never prints "TG3: rx#N ARP" ? RX/VLAN bug.
   If Mac never replies ? Sharing ignores static; need DHCP or ARP inject.

   Manual gateway MAC (from ifconfig ether on bridge100 / USB NIC):
	#include "StartShare"
   then before Ping, or edit below:
	U8 gmac[6]; gmac[0]=0x..; ... ARPCachePut(0xC0A80201, gmac);
*/
Cd(__DIR__);;
#include "Load"
"==== StartShare: static via macOS Internet Sharing ====\n";
NetStaticConfigure("192.168.2.50", "192.168.2.1", "255.255.255.0");
NetRep;
"\nPinging 192.168.2.1 (any key to stop)...\n";
"Watch for: TG3: rx#N ARP   then   Received reply\n\n";
Ping("192.168.2.1");
